<title>INDIA: India M Scooters up 6.6 pct, bonus hopes.</title>
<headline>India M Scooters up 6.6 pct, bonus hopes.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Maharashtra Scooters Ltd rose sharply in early trade on Wednesday after the company said it plans to issue bonus equity shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>The company said on Tuesday it has convened a board meeting on May 7 to consider a bonus issue and finalise accounts and recommend dividend for the year ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The share jumped 14.10 rupees, or 6.6 percent, to 227.75 on the National Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Trading on the Bombay exchange was delayed on Wednesday due to a technical problem.</p>
<p>The company is part of the scooter giant Bajaj Auto group.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
